{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Symptom\n\n`_metered_spend()` in `infra/terraform/bedrock-spend-cap/handler.py` accumulates token spend across regions, but a single CloudWatch `ClientError` returns `None` from lines 316-318 or 329-331, discarding totals already collected from healthy regions.\n\n## Code facts from `origin/main`\n\nBoth cited paths resolve under `origin/main`: `infra/terraform/bedrock-spend-cap/handler.py` and `tests/infra/test_bedrock_spend_cap_handler.py`.\n\n`_metered_spend()` builds per-region CloudWatch queries at lines 283-315, prices token data into `total` at lines 332-337, returns `0.0` when no per-model series exists at lines 338-340, then returns `total` at line 341. The only production call site is `infra/terraform/bedrock-spend-cap/handler.py:477`.\n\n`handler()` consumes the result at the CE-poll trigger on line 493, unavailable handling at lines 507-514, display/log text at lines 523-540, the release guard at line 562, and the attach path at line 570. Existing tests already cover whole CloudWatch listing failure returning `None` at `tests/infra/test_bedrock_spend_cap_handler.py:357-367` and whole data failure returning `None` at `:370-394`. They do not cover a later-region failure after a healthy region contributes a partial total. The current `FakeAWS.client()` returns the same CloudWatch fake for every region at `:176-187`, so partial-region tests need a region-aware CloudWatch fake.\n\nOther `_metered_spend` references found in `origin/main`: monkeypatch helpers at `tests/infra/test_bedrock_spend_cap_handler.py:249` and `:254`; direct unit calls at `:363`, `:390`, `:433`, `:889`, and `:919`.\n\n## Sequencing after 604c-ade8\n\nThis ticket is sequenced after sibling ticket `604c-ade8`, which is already certified, claimed, and touching the same handler file first. That plan removes the unconditional `metered is None` CE-poll trigger from line 493. It keeps only the due interval plus near-threshold metered-spend triggers so a metered outage cannot override `CE_MIN_INTERVAL_SECONDS`.\n\nCfe0 must not reintroduce `metered is None`, `metered.degraded`, or any equivalent unconditional degraded-meter trigger at line 493. A degraded partial must not force the near-threshold branch merely because it is degraded; that would recreate the per-tick CE hammering that 604c removes. The post-604c gate should stay conceptually `due or (metered is not None and metered_total * 5 >= THRESHOLD_USD * 4)`, with cfe0 adapting `metered_total` to `MeteredSpend.total`.\n\nThe arithmetic risk is explicit: `MeteredSpend.total` is a lower bound, so the near-threshold test can be false while full regional spend would be true. That is the trade-off created by 604c's interval policy. Cfe0 handles it by carrying `degraded=True` into release safety and operator visibility: degraded partials block release, expose the failed regions, still attach when the observed partial reaches the cap, and rely on the due CE interval for the next authoritative read.\n\n## Design\n\nUse a small result object, not a bare float: `MeteredSpend(total: float, degraded: bool, failures: tuple[MeteredFailure, ...])`, where each `MeteredFailure` stores `region` and `exception_class`. If at least 1 token series contributes before or after a regional `ClientError`, return `MeteredSpend(total=<partial>, degraded=True, failures=...)`. If no token series contributes before a CloudWatch `ClientError` prevents a complete scan, keep the unavailable path by returning `None`.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] `infra/terraform/bedrock-spend-cap/handler.py` defines `MeteredSpend`.\n- [ ] `MeteredSpend.total` stores the numeric CloudWatch dollar total.\n- [ ] `MeteredSpend.degraded` is `True` when at least 1 region raises `ClientError` during the scan.\n- [ ] `MeteredSpend.failures` stores each failed region name.\n- [ ] `MeteredSpend.failures` stores each failed exception class.\n- [ ] `_metered_spend()` returns a degraded `MeteredSpend` after one region contributes token spend then a later region raises during `list_metrics`.\n- [ ] `_metered_spend()` returns a degraded `MeteredSpend` after one region contributes token spend then a later region raises during `get_metric_data`.\n- [ ] `_metered_spend()` continues scanning later regions after an earlier region raises `ClientError`.\n- [ ] When a CloudWatch `ClientError` prevents a complete scan before any token series contributes, `_metered_spend()` returns `None`.\n- [ ] Degraded-region logging includes the failed region name.\n- [ ] Degraded-region logging includes the exception class name.\n- [ ] The CE-poll gate uses `MeteredSpend.total` for near-threshold arithmetic.\n- [ ] A degraded partial below the near-threshold amount does not poll CE before the due interval.\n- [ ] A degraded partial at the near-threshold amount polls CE before the due interval.\n- [ ] The CE-poll gate contains no unconditional `metered.degraded` trigger.\n- [ ] The CE-poll gate contains no unconditional `metered is None` trigger reintroduced by cfe0.\n- [ ] `signal_unavailable` is `True` when `MeteredSpend.degraded` is `True`.\n- [ ] A degraded partial with `total >= THRESHOLD_USD` attaches the deny policy when it is not attached.\n- [ ] A degraded partial with `total < THRESHOLD_USD` leaves an existing deny policy attached.\n- [ ] A degraded partial with `total < THRESHOLD_USD` publishes no release notification.\n- [ ] Metered log text reports the numeric partial total when `MeteredSpend.degraded` is `True`.\n- [ ] `tests/infra/test_bedrock_spend_cap_handler.py` extends `FakeAWS.client()` so CloudWatch fakes can vary by `region_name`.\n- [ ] `tests/infra/test_bedrock_spend_cap_handler.py::test_metered_spend_preserves_partial_total_when_later_region_listing_fails` covers the listing-failure partial.\n- [ ] `tests/infra/test_bedrock_spend_cap_handler.py::test_metered_spend_preserves_partial_total_when_later_region_data_fails` covers the data-failure partial.\n- [ ] `tests/infra/test_bedrock_spend_cap_handler.py::test_metered_spend_records_degraded_region_failure` covers region name logging.\n- [ ] `tests/infra/test_bedrock_spend_cap_handler.py::test_metered_spend_records_degraded_region_failure` covers exception class logging.\n- [ ] `tests/infra/test_bedrock_spend_cap_handler.py::test_degraded_partial_meter_below_near_threshold_respects_ce_interval` covers the non-due no-poll case.\n- [ ] `tests/infra/test_bedrock_spend_cap_handler.py::test_degraded_partial_meter_at_near_threshold_polls_ce` covers the near-threshold poll case.\n- [ ] `tests/infra/test_bedrock_spend_cap_handler.py::test_degraded_partial_meter_can_attach` covers fail-closed attachment.\n- [ ] `tests/infra/test_bedrock_spend_cap_handler.py::test_degraded_partial_meter_cannot_release` covers release blocking.\n- [ ] `tests/infra/test_bedrock_spend_cap_handler.py::test_metered_spend_cloudwatch_failure_before_any_series_reports_unavailable` covers the `None` fallback.\n- [ ] `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" pytest tests/infra/test_bedrock_spend_cap_handler.py` exits 0.\n- [ ] `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" make verify` exits 0.\n\n## Testing\n\nDuring development, run `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" pytest tests/infra/test_bedrock_spend_cap_handler.py -k 'metered_spend or degraded_partial_meter'`. Before push, run `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" pytest tests/infra/test_bedrock_spend_cap_handler.py`, then `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" make verify`.\n\n## Source\n\nRaised from Gerrit change 2984 patchset 7 review feedback, then narrowed to preserve partial CloudWatch totals without weakening 604c's CE polling interval or release safety."}},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1789877954183182862,"uuid":"4f3727e6-fe64-403d-8fd0-5543f458e4e5"}